@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "downloads"

Feature: Downloads Permissioning
	Testing the Permissioning of the Downloads portlet.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen DWN Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENDWNA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen DWN Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View dxp downloads as permissioned users
	DXP downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen DWN Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENDWNA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENDWNA"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.3" product and "Product/Service Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.3 and Liferay Commerce 3.0 (Test)" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.3" product and "Product/Service Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.3 and Liferay Commerce 3.0 (Test)" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible

Scenario: View portal downloads as permissioned users
	Portal downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen DWN Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENDWNA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENDWNA"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Portal"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Portal"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-10-15 Portal-171" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-06-25 Portal-170" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-12-17 Portal-71" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-08-21 Portal-70" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2015-12-17 Hotfix-1285" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2013-01-14 All-1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 5.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 5.2 EE SP5 Update 2011-02-24" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-10-15 Portal-171" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.2 EE Update 2019-06-25 Portal-170" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-12-17 Portal-71" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.1 EE GA3 Update 2018-08-21 Portal-70" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 6.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2015-12-17 Hotfix-1285" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Portal 6.0 EE SP2 Update 2013-01-14 All-1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "Portal 5.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Portal 5.2 EE SP5 Update 2011-02-24" should be visible

Scenario: View enterprise search downloads as permissioned users
	Enterprise search downloads should be visible according to the permissions that users have.

	Given I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen DWN Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENDWNA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I assign a user the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENDWNA"
	And I add an order with the product "Enterprise Search - Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENDWNA"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Liferay Enterprise Search"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - Liferay Enterprise Search"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Enterprise Search" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.1" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.0" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch Downloads" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Enterprise Search Standard" should not be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch 6 Downloads" should not be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dwn.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "Enterprise Search" product and "Product" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.1" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay Enterprise Search for Liferay DXP 7.0" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch Downloads" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Enterprise Search Standard" should not be visible
	And the download with the name "Elasticsearch 6 Downloads" should not be visible

Scenario: View enterprise search downloads as enterprise search standard permissioned users
	Enterprise search downloads should be visible according to the permissions that enterprise search standard users have.

	Given I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dwn.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dwn.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DWN                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
